attempts.raw:
@start **The window opens on a single spine column.** Column 0, `yedI`, is carried by 100% of chromosomes, all persistent, in a region of plasticity in 0% of calls {S1}. The model names 99% of them, at 0.05 bits {S1, M}.

@variable **The rest of the window is fork and variable columns**, 1 to 79, carried by 9 to 88%, 71 persistent and 8 shell, in a region of plasticity in 0.2 to 35% of calls {S2}. The `fliR` to `fliE` genes, columns 7 to 20, are [[flagellar biosynthesis]] {S2.c7-20, Q, X}. A branch of 4 shell families runs through columns 21 to 24, `emrE` to `insQ`, in 14 to 34% {S2.b21}.

@model **The model names more genes on the spine column than on the fork and variable ones**, 99 against 88%, and hesitates less there, 0.05 against 0.52 bits {M}. Its most hesitant column, 21, `yedK`, is a fork column, at 1.59 bits {H, M}.

@end **The window ends on a fork column.** Column 79, `cmoA`, is carried by 32% of chromosomes {S2.c79, E}. It is not rare: in the other chromosomes it lies beyond the window's end {T}.

@whole **Across the window it names 88% of genes**, 0.52 bits on average, perplexity 2.0 families {G}. Inside a region of plasticity it hesitates more than outside, 1.90 against 0.24 bits, and names fewer genes, 57% against 94% {C}.

